Check Hadoop version 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop version 

List files and directories in HDFS 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -ls 

List directories under HDFS root 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -ls / 

Copy a file from local filesystem to HDFS 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ cat > students.txt 
1,kriti,cse,45 
2,neha,ece,56 
3,jyothi,ce,78 
4,priya,mechanical,89 
  
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ cat students.txt 

[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -copyFromLocal students.txt /user/cloudera

Copy a local file to HDFS using put 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -put students.txt /user/cloudera/studentscopied.txt

  Copy a file from HDFS to local filesystem 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -copyToLocal students.txt  studentscopiedtolocal.txt

Check HDFS health 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hdfs fsck / 

Create a directory in HDFS 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -mkdir kriti2018 

Copy a file within HDFS 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -mkdir -p kriti2018 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -cp students.txt kriti2018 

Create an empty HDFS file 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -touchz empty.txt 

Check the size of an HDFS file 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -du -s students.txt

Print the contents of an HDFS file 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -cat students.txt

Count files and directories 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -count kriti2018 

Remove a file from HDFS 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -rm empty.txt 

Delete an HDFS directory completely 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -rm -r kriti2018 

Copy files within HDFS using cp 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -mkdir kriti2018 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -cp students.txt kriti2018 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -ls kriti2018 

Move a file in HDFS 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -touchz emptyfile.txt 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -mv emptyfile.txt kriti2018 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -ls kriti2018 

Get help for an individual command 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hdfs dfs -usage mkdir 

Get help for HDFS commands 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -help 
Usage: hadoop fs [generic options] 
[-appendToFile <localsrc> ... <dst>] 

Check HDFS memory/storage status 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -df 

Check cluster balancing 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop balancer 

Change permissions to 777 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -ls -r 

[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -chmod 777 /user/cloudera/studentscopied.txt 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -ls -r 

empty hdfs trash
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -expunge 

Display the last kilobyte of a file 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -tail /user/cloudera/students.txt 

Append a local file to an HDFS file 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ echo "This is the first file." > first.txt 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ echo "This is the second file." > second.txt 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -copyFromLocal second.txt /user/cloudera/ 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -appendToFile /home/cloudera/Desktop/first.txt 
/user/cloudera/second.txt 
[cloudera@quickstart Desktop]$ hadoop fs -cat /user/cloudera/second.txt 



  
